/* ============================================================================
   mortgage-rate.epher -- the interest rate a given payment implies, and the
   difference between the quoted (APR) rate and the effective annual rate

   The finance builtin tvm_i solves the annuity equation for the per-period
   rate: given the term, principal (negative) and payment, it returns the
   monthly rate i. Multiplying by 12 gives the nominal annual rate, the way
   lenders quote an APR; compounding that monthly rate for a year gives the
   higher effective annual rate (1+i)^12 - 1. Source: standard TVM
   formulas; see Kellison, The Theory of Interest, chapters 2-3.

   Accuracy: 12 displayed digits; tvm_i bisects the rate to about 1e-15.

   Run it from a terminal:
     Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/finance/loans/mortgage-rate.epher
     Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\finance\loans\mortgage-rate.epher"
     macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/finance/loans/mortgage-rate.epher

   The knobs to edit are in the knob section; everything after it is
   machinery you can leave alone.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- knobs ------------------------------------------------------------------
const principal = 200000    // loan amount at closing, USD
const payment = 1500        // monthly payment offered, USD
const years = 30            // term in years

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
i = tvm_i(years * 12, -principal, payment, 0)   // monthly rate the payment implies
print("monthly rate:", i)
print("nominal annual rate (APR, 12 x monthly):", 12 * i)
print("effective annual rate (1+i)^12 - 1:", (1 + i) ^ 12 - 1)
// The gap between 8.232% and 8.550% is monthly compounding: interest added
// every month earns interest itself. The quoted APR is the nominal 8.232%;
// the effective rate is what a year of that compounding truly costs.
/* ---- expected output ----
= 200000
= 1500
= 30
= 0.00685998148446
= monthly rate: 0.00685998148446
= nominal annual rate (APR, 12 x monthly): 0.0823197778135
= effective annual rate (1+i)^12 - 1: 0.0854978247676
*/
